Lunchtime is approaching.
My Saturday shift has now ended.
I take off my apron and fold it.
Today I learned to do many new things in the café.
My first day was very good.
I go over to Sunita tai.
"Sunita tai, thank you very much for your patience," I say.
"Today you taught me a lot."
Sunita tai smiles warmly.
"You did very good work today, Maya," she says.
"Let's meet again next Saturday."
I take her leave and step out of the café.
My flat is quite close to the café.
I set off to go home on foot.
My legs are aching and I am very tired.
But I am very happy on the inside.
I learned to talk to new people.
I feel proud to have served this community.
